  "id": "vedanta",
  "term": "Vedanta",
  "definition": "Vedanta, as described here in the form of Advaita Vedanta, is an Indian philosophical tradition that questions the idea of a fixed, enduring self-identity. In this psychology context, it is used as a perspective for understanding self-related experience, meta-awareness, and changes in self-experience linked to meditation.",
